course: dictionary
lesson: 14810
title: Claimed, not proved
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you whether something is really true. Purportedly is one of them. It means according to what people say or claim, though it may not be true.
explain: «The letter was purportedly written by the queen.» The writer does not say the queen wrote it. The word tells you that this is only what is claimed, and nobody has proved it yet.
explain: News writers often use this word to be careful. When you read purportedly, slow down, check the facts, and look for proof before you believe it.
fact: Purportedly is an adverb, a formal word that tells you how something is said to be.
fact: «Purportedly» means according to what is claimed, though it may not be true.
fact: «Purportedly» is a signal word: it warns you that a claim still needs checking.
fact: A good check is to swap in the words «it is claimed that» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The message was purportedly sent by the head teacher.» What does purportedly tell you? | The message is very long | *It is claimed the head teacher sent it, but this is not proved | The head teacher definitely sent it | The head teacher is very cross
exercise: Mia reads, «The film is purportedly the best ever made.» What should Mia do? | *Check the facts, because purportedly means it is only claimed | Skip the whole article | Share it with everyone at once | Believe it straight away, because it is in the news
exercise: Which phrase means the same as purportedly? | *it is claimed that | it is certain that | it is definitely true that | it is funny that
test: «The treasure was purportedly buried under the old oak tree.» What does this sentence tell the reader? | The reader must dig at once | The oak tree is very tall | The treasure has been found and proved | *People say the treasure is buried there, but it may not be true
test: Which sentence shows a claim that may not be true? | «The sky is blue on a clear day.» | «Water boils at 100 degrees.» | «Two plus two is four.» | *«The phone was purportedly found in a bin.»
exam: «The dragon was purportedly seen over the lake, but nobody took a photo.» Why should a careful reader doubt this? | Because lakes are too wet for dragons | Because the sentence has no full stop | *Because purportedly tells us it is only claimed, and there is no proof | Dragons are never seen anywhere
